@.str.126 = private unnamed_addr constant [4797 x i8] c"\0AParse PROTO_FILES and generate output based on the options given:\0A  -IPATH, --proto_path=PATH   Specify the directory in which to search for\0A                              imports.  May be specified multiple times;\0A                              directories will be searched in order.  If not\0A                              given, the current working directory is used.\0A                              If not found in any of the these directories,\0A                              the --descriptor_set_in descriptors will be\0A                              checked for required proto file.\0A  --version                   Show version info and exit.\0A  -h, --help                  Show this text and exit.\0A  --encode=MESSAGE_TYPE       Read a text-format message of the given type\0A                              from standard input and write it in binary\0A                              to standard output.  The message type must\0A                              be defined in PROTO_FILES or their imports.\0A  --deterministic_output      When using --encode, ensure map fields are\0A                              deterministically ordered. Note that this order\0A                              is not canonical, and changes across builds or\0A                              releases of protoc.\0A  --decode=MESSAGE_TYPE       Read a binary message of the given type from\0A                              standard input and write it in text format\0A                              to standard output.  The message type must\0A                              be defined in PROTO_FILES or their imports.\0A  --decode_raw                Read an arbitrary protocol message from\0A                              standard input and write the raw tag/value\0A                              pairs in text format to standard output.  No\0A                              PROTO_FILES should be given when using this\0A                              flag.\0A  --descriptor_set_in=FILES   Specifies a delimited list of FILES\0A                              each containing a FileDescriptorSet (a\0A                              protocol buffer defined in descriptor.proto).\0A                              The FileDescriptor for each of the PROTO_FILES\0A                              provided will be loaded from these\0A                              FileDescriptorSets. If a FileDescriptor\0A                              appears multiple times, the first occurrence\0A                              will be used.\0A  -oFILE,                     Writes a FileDescriptorSet (a protocol buffer,\0A    --descriptor_set_out=FILE defined in descriptor.proto) containing all of\0A                              the input files to FILE.\0A  --include_imports           When using --descriptor_set_out, also include\0A                              all dependencies of the input files in the\0A                              set, so that the set is self-contained.\0A  --include_source_info       When using --descriptor_set_out, do not strip\0A                              SourceCodeInfo from the FileDescriptorProto.\0A                              This results in vastly larger descriptors that\0A                              include information about the original\0A                              location of each decl in the source file as\0A                              well as surrounding comments.\0A  --retain_options            When using --descriptor_set_out, do not strip\0A                              any options from the FileDescriptorProto.\0A                              This results in potentially larger descriptors\0A                              that include information about options that were\0A                              only meant to be useful during compilation.\0A  --dependency_out=FILE       Write a dependency output file in the format\0A                              expected by make. This writes the transitive\0A                              set of input file paths to FILE\0A  --error_format=FORMAT       Set the format in which to print errors.\0A                              FORMAT may be 'gcc' (the default) or 'msvs'\0A                              (Microsoft Visual Studio format).\0A  --fatal_warnings            Make warnings be fatal (similar to -Werr in\0A                              gcc). This flag will make protoc return\0A                              with a non-zero exit code if any warnings\0A                              are generated.\0A  --print_free_field_numbers  Print the free field numbers of the messages\0A                              defined in the given proto files. Extension ranges\0A                              are counted as occupied fields numbers.\0A  --enable_codegen_trace      Enables tracing which parts of protoc are\0A                              responsible for what codegen output. Not supported\0A                              by all backends or on all platforms.\00", align 1
